=begin
	   OSACommander Version: '4.1.9 (November 1, 2026)
	
	   Usage: 
	
	   ;osacommander info <ship type>                       Will gather your ship info and save your current ship type
	   ;osacommander crew                                   Will display commands for auto crew login
	   ;osacommander begin                                  Will go to bank to withdrawl silvers retrieve your ship and get underway
	   ;osacommander undead                                 Orders crew to start undead combat scripts
	   ;osacommander bless                                  Will begin a blessing sequence for your crew
	   ;osacommander start                                  Orders crew to start combat scripts
	   ;osacommander end                                    Orders crew to begin end sequence after enemy ship is cleared
	   ;osacommander stop                                   Orders crew to stop all combat scripts and resets ship boarding settings
	   ;osacommander exit                                   Orders crew to attention and to exit game
	   ;osacommander pause                                  Pauses crew combat scripts
	   ;osacommander setup                                  Opens Setup Menu For Commander
	   ;osacommander unpause                                Unpauses crew combat scripts
	   ;osacommander sheath                                 Orders crew to sheath thier weapons
	   ;osacommander testcon <crew member>                  Orders a crew member to respond. For testing thier settings and connection
	   ;osacommander kick <crew member                      Commands a crew member to depart from duty
	   ;osacommander unkick <crew member                    Commands a crew member to return to duty
	   ;osacommander muster                                 Takes a roll call of your crew members
	   ;osacommander muster count                           Will determine who present is not of the ships company
	   ;osacommander broadcast                              This will look ocean and broadcast the ships location and accept or decline any request to join
	   ;osacommander summon                                 Call your crew to your location, they will then salute and join your group
	   ;osacommander underway                               Orders crew to get ship underway
	   ;osacommander repairs                                Orders crew to do repairs
	   ;osacommander return                                 Turns off detection and returns to port, also does broadcast to set location and bring on new crew
	   ;osacommander bread                                  Medical Officer will make mana bread and share it with everyone with Groupspellup checked
	   ;osacommander spells                                 Orders crew to begin spellups
	   ;osacommander spellup                                Orders crew to perform a mana spellup
	   ;osacommander spellup <name>                         Orders crew to spellup a specific individual
	   ;osacommander silvers                                Orders crew to give all silvers to the commander
	   ;osacommander status                                 Orders crew to display status info in crew chat
	   ;osacommander resource                               Orders crew to display resource info in crew chat
	   ;osacommander gemstone                               Orders crew to display gemstone info in crew chat
	   ;osacommander task                                   Orders crew to turn in and get new tasks
	   ;osacommander task count                             Will determine who hasn't rogered up
	   ;osacommander sell                                   Orders crew to sell thier loot and return when finished
	   ;osacommander reset                                  Orders crew to reset osacrew scripts
	   ;osacommander update <scriptname>                    Orders crew to update a script
	   ;osacommander detection on/off                       Turns on or off your enemy ship detection
	   ;osacommander cleanup on/off                         Turns on or off detection of the death of the Captain for straggler cleanup
	   ;osacommander cleanup                                Begins the cleanup process
	   ;osacommander scripted on/off                        Turns on or off acceptance of outside scripted crew members
	   ;osacommander noscript on/off                        Turns on or off a pause for non-scripting members of crew to do tasks and deposit silver
	   ;osacommander poaching on/off                        Turns on or off the anti-poaching feature for you and your crew. 
	   ;osacommander checkversion                           Checks the version of all scripts for you and your crew members
	   ;osacommander combat                                 Tells entire crew to start OSACombat.
	   ;osacommander combat <name>                          Tells a specific crew member to start OSACombat.
	   ;osacommander loot <name>                            Tells a specific crew member to turn on looting and the rest to turn off looting.
	   ;osacommander help                                   Shows this list of commands
	   ;osacommander checkpoint                             Shows the saved encounter checkpoint (stage, enemy ship and how long ago)
	   ;osacommander resume                                 Continues the current encounter from its last saved checkpoint
	   ;osacommander resume force                           Resumes even if the checkpoint is more than 30 minutes old
	   osacommander setup|help|checkpoint                   (no semicolon) Same commands, typed while osacommander is running
	
	   This is the OSA Commander script. It is ran from your ship captain to give orders to the crew. 
	   Enjoy 
	
	   ~Peggyanne 
	 PS: feel free to send me any bugs via discord Bait#4376 and I'll try my best to fix them.
	 
	 Change Log:
	 
        September 20, 2026 - Sever spellup now does the same prep as a normal spellup first: armor adjustments, mana
                             spellup when needed, self ewaggle and armor specializations. Added a Mana Spellup
                             Threshold (minutes, default 60) in place of the old fixed check.
        September 28, 2026 - Sever spellup no longer announces completion early. Task Complete reports are collected
                             by a listener, counted once per mustered crew member, with a 10 minute limit and a
                             running "x/y - waiting on" count.
           October 2, 2026 - Every Task Complete wait shares one script-long listener with the running count, and
                             names who never reported on a timeout. The commander's own sever spellup runs alongside
                             the crew's.
           October 4, 2026 - Setup-window methods renamed to commander_* so the OSA scripts stop overwriting each
                             other's windows.
          October 10, 2026 - Every method shared with another OSA script now has a commander_ prefix (one shared Ruby
                             namespace), so osacrew's copies no longer replace osacommander's. Saves refresh the
                             in-memory settings.
          October 11, 2026 - The exit recite reads the ship name from osacommander's settings.
          October 25, 2026 - A task round starts when the order is sent, so waits no longer count the last round's
                             reports. Added encounter checkpoints (1 Detected to 10 Stats, S Sunk) with ;osacommander
                             checkpoint, resume and resume force; steps that must not repeat are guarded. setup, help
                             and checkpoint can be typed without a semicolon.
          October 28, 2026 - Fixed weapon blesses never running before undead encounters and granting a crew request
                             erroring. Anchor and sails retry after roundtime, and ShowRoomID is only turned off when
                             no other OSA script needs it. Sever checks the muster first and shows the running count
                             while the commander casts.
          October 31, 2026 - Ship mapping is one table (COMMANDER_SHIPS): only your ship is tagged and moves go by
                             room number. Cleanup reworked: sweep the enemy ship room by room (fight, loot, listen),
                             then walk your ship pausing 1.5 seconds a room for hidden pirates, with an ambush watcher
                             and a 10 sweep limit.
          November 1, 2026 - Fixed the end-of-encounter spellup never happening (it read a stale saved average). It
                             now uses your current spells and runs with one crew member or more. With no crew mustered
                             you spell up yourself (mana spellup, then ewaggle). A message shows the average and the
                             setting either way.
=end 

def commander_load_yaml_file(path)
	return {} unless File.exist?(path)
	raw = File.read(path)
	return {} if raw.strip.empty?
	(YAML.safe_load(raw, permitted_classes: [Time, Symbol], aliases: true) || {}).transform_keys(&:to_s)
rescue StandardError
	{}
end

def commander_osacommander_data
	commander_load_yaml_file(File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, "osacommander.yaml"))
end

def commander_osacrew_data
	commander_load_yaml_file(File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, "osacrew.yaml"))
end

def commander_osacombat_data
	commander_load_yaml_file(File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, "osacombat.yaml"))
end

def sail2_data
	commander_load_yaml_file(File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, "sail2.yaml"))
end

def commander_save_to_commander(key, value, push: false)
	self.class.commander_save_to_commander(key, value, push: push)
	@commander_data = self.class.commander_osacommander_data
end

def commander_save_to_crew(key, value, push: false)
	self.class.commander_save_to_crew(key, value, push: push)
	@crew_data = self.class.commander_osacrew_data
end

def commander_save_to_combat(key, value, push: false)
	self.class.commander_save_to_combat(key, value, push: push)
	@combat_data[key.to_s] = self.class.commander_osacombat_data[key.to_s] if @combat_data.is_a?(Hash)
end

def commander_lnet_crew(msg)
	crew_channel = commander_osacrew_data["crew"]
	if crew_channel.nil? || crew_channel.strip.empty?
		respond "--- OSACommander: Crew channel is not defined. Please run ;osacrew setup and set your Crew Channel before continuing."
		return
	end
	# Every crew order (except mana requests) starts a new Task Complete round. Stamped here, at
	# send time, so a commander_task_complete called right after this can't count reports left
	# over from the previous round.
	$osa_task_round_start = Time.now unless msg.to_s =~ /^I Need .* Mana!/
	LNet.send_message(attr = { 'type' => 'channel', 'channel' => crew_channel }, msg)
end

# Checks for required scripts and prompts the user to download any that are missing.
# deps is an array of hashes: [{ name: 'scriptname', author: 'author' }, ...]
def commander_check_dependencies(script_label, deps)
	deps.each do |dep|
		next if Script.exists?(dep[:name])
		respond ""
		respond " =========================================================="
		respond "  #{script_label} requires: #{dep[:name]}"
		respond "  This script could not be found in your script folder."
		respond " =========================================================="
		respond "  Would you like to download it now?"
		respond "    1. Yes - download #{dep[:name]} and continue"
		respond "    2. No  - exit (#{script_label} cannot run without it)"
		respond " =========================================================="
		respond "  Please select an option - ;send <#>"
		respond ""
		clear
		answer = nil
		answer = get until answer.to_s.strip =~ /^[12]$/
		if answer.strip == "1"
			respond "  Downloading #{dep[:name]}..."
			args = ["download", dep[:name]]
			args << "--author=#{dep[:author]}" if dep[:author]
			start_script("repository", args)
			wait_until { !running?("repository") }
			respond "  Download complete."
			respond ""
		else
			respond "  Very well. Please restart #{script_label} once you have #{dep[:name]} installed."
			exit
		end
	end
end

